  "body": "Viewing By Private Appointment. \r\n\r\nNew CV just updated ($960,000) to include newly issued COA for the downstairs area. \r\n\r\n\r\n2 Separate Living Areas. 2 Double Bedrooms. 2 Bathrooms. 2 Parking Spaces. Beautiful garden. \r\n\r\nIt’s the perfect time to buy! \r\n\r\nWith two up and one down this is an ideal home for those starting on the property ladder (rooms for flatmates to assist with the mortgage) or overseas parents coming to stay, teenagers ( part and full time) or an ideal work from home office as it has its own access/ ensuite facilities and tea room area. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis elevated brick and block property, is walking distance to Rothesay Bay Beach, offering the perfect blend of relaxed living and future potential.\r\n\r\nStep inside to warm open plan spaces with a generous outdoor area - perfect for weekend BBQs, morning coffee, or sunset drinks.\r\n\r\nBut the real surprise is out the back - a lush garden oasis bursting with over thirteen established fruit trees - from banana, peach, feijoa and pomegranate to double-grafted plum and more. There's even your own veggie garden, so you can live the good life, right at home.\r\n\r\nThe interior has been freshened up for market, but there's still room to add your own flair over time - whether you're a first-home buyer, creative soul, or someone looking to secure a slice of this sought-after seaside suburb.\r\n\r\nWith character and beach lifestyle promise, this home is ideal for those starting out, slowing down, or ready to make a move. All just moments from local cafes, shops, schools and public transport. \r\n\r\nHappy to conjunct! \r\n\r\nProperty Files- https://www.harcourtsfiles.co.nz/listings/LB73",
